# =====================================================================================
# What is NOT committed, and why. Everything here is large, regenerable, or
# machine-specific. See publishable/PROVISIONING.md for how to restore each one.
#
# NOTE: git does NOT support trailing comments on a pattern line. A line like
#   engine/        # 1.2 GB bundle
# is parsed as a literal pattern including the spaces and the comment, and silently
# matches nothing. Every comment below is on its own line for that reason.
# =====================================================================================

# ---- vendored / provisioned, never committed ----------------------------------------
# engine/ is a ~1.2 GB bundle and additionally contains a HAND-COPIED pypdf inside its
# embedded interpreter, which is not manifest-reproducible (PROVISIONING.md section 3).
.venv/
engine/
../rocketride-server/

# ---- corpora: ~5.9 GB, rebuildable --------------------------------------------------
# GovDocs1 PDFs (public domain, digitalcorpora.org); mt10k rebuildable from the manifest.
corpus/
data/
pdftest/

# ---- run state and logs: per-machine, contain absolute paths ------------------------
logs/
weekend_logs/
repl_logs/
# Checkpoints ARE evidence — the RSS series behind every memory claim lives here, and the
# meeting artifact cites two of them directly. 604 KB for both directories. Only the
# ephemeral markers are excluded.
weekend_state/*.tmp
weekend_state/*.done
repl_state/*.tmp
repl_state/*.done
docker/out/
status.txt
repl_status.txt
# heartbeat for the matched-layer sweep; rewritten every few seconds
sweep_status.txt
# partial/tmp sweep checkpoints must never land; completed cells are committed deliberately
# after the run, matching the repl_state/ and weekend_state/ precedent
sweep_state/*.tmp
sweep_state/*.done
weekend_run.log
nohup.out

# ---- regenerable harness output -----------------------------------------------------
working/pipes/generated/
working/results/selftest/

# ---- model weights and caches -------------------------------------------------------
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.onnx
# *.pth added 2026-08-27: rf-detr-base.pth (372 MB) appeared at the repo root and at
# working/video/probe/ during the reader-equivalence proof; a checkpoint must never
# enter the repo — identity is the md5 read-back (RFDETR_BASE_MD5), not the bytes.
*.pth
.cache/
huggingface/

# ---- environment files ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The current .env holds only a local URI and the placeholder key MYAPIKEY, i.e. nothing
# secret today. It is excluded anyway: the moment someone puts a real key in it, the habit
# of committing it would leak. .env.example is committed instead.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- python / os --------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# ---- kept deliberately --------------------------------------------------------------
# working/results/*.json IS committed: it is the evidence behind every claim and is small.
# *.jsonl is therefore NOT globally ignored; the one large one (the corpus manifest) is
# already excluded by corpus/ above.
